The given inequality is $|x + y + z| + |x + y - z| + |x - y + z| + |-x + y + z| \le 4$.

By the triangle inequality, we have
\begin{align*}
|x + y + z| + |x + y - z| + |x - y + z| + |-x + y + z| &\le |(x + y + z) + (x + y - z) + (x - y + z) + (-x + y + z)| \\
&= |3y + 3x| \\
&= 3|x + y|.
\end{align*}

Therefore, we have $3|x + y| \le 4$, which implies $|x + y| \le \frac{4}{3}$.

We can visualize the region given by the inequality as a pyramid with a square base. The base is a square with side length $\sqrt{2}$, and the height of the pyramid is $\frac{4}{3}$.

The volume of the pyramid is given by $\frac{1}{3} \cdot \text{base area} \cdot \text{height} = \frac{1}{3} \cdot (\sqrt{2})^2 \cdot \frac{4}{3} = \boxed{\frac{8}{9}}$.The answer is: \frac{8}{9}
